#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Batch 6: establishing views, fourth pass (v4). Land first, life small and zoned, one backlight, raised viewpoint, plain areas, no clones.
R = '/home/user/workspace/r3/prompts'
HEAD = "A wide 16:9 landscape frame from a big-budget natural-history film about an alien world, shot on location. It must read as real {night}photography of a real place, not artwork: {cam}, true lens perspective, natural light only, {haze}, {grain}, restrained natural colour."
CALM = "RESTRAINT. This is a calm, wide establishing frame. The land and the weather are the subject. Big simple shapes; wide areas of plain {plain}. Life is sparse and small in the frame and sits in zones where it would really grow, never spread evenly over everything. Nothing is repeated: every {things} differs from the others in size, shape, state and angle, and some are broken, some empty, some half hidden."
TAIL = "It must feel like a place you could walk into and keep walking: firm ground at your feet, a readable route into the middle distance, far landmarks dissolving in the air, the land plainly continuing beyond every edge of the frame. Nothing posed, nothing centred, no painterly brushwork, no illustration or game-art styling. No people, no buildings or ruins, no cameras, drones or equipment, no text, no watermark, no border."
A = [HEAD.format(night='', cam='24 mm lens, deep focus', haze='humid haze building with distance', grain='slight film grain'),
"""THE PLACE. The inside of the windpipe of a creature the size of a mountain range that died ages ago. It is now a tunnel-cave about two hundred metres high and wide that runs away into the distance, gently curving. Its walls and roof are dark wet rock crossed by great hoops of pale cartilage, each as thick as a house, so the tunnel is ribbed like the inside of a hose; but the hoops are ancient: stained, cracked, some sagging, some fallen, some half buried under flowstone, moss and hanging roots. At intervals the roof has fallen in, leaving ragged skylights. Through each skylight the sun comes down in one shaft through the wet air, and under each shaft an island of rainforest has grown on the rubble. A river runs along the tunnel floor. The tunnel breathes: a slow tongue of cloud slides along under the roof.""",
"""VIEWPOINT AND LAYOUT, asymmetric. Seen from a ledge of fallen blocks about fifteen metres above the river, in the dark stretch of tunnel well before the first skylight, so most of the frame is in cool shadow. The river runs from the bottom left away down the tunnel: the route. The first forest island is three hundred metres away, right of centre, standing in its shaft of sun: its trees are tiny under the vast roof, a mixed forest of tree ferns, pale-trunked trees with flat dark red crowns and tall bare-stemmed giants, with one thread of waterfall falling from the skylight beside it. Small flyers circle in the shaft as specks. At the river's edge near the island a herd of six-legged grazing animals drinks, tiny from here. Far beyond, much smaller and paler in the haze, a second shaft falls on a second island, and a third is only a glimmer. On the ledge in the lower right corner, in shadow, lies the old carcass of one of the grazers, sunk in moss; a patch of pale leathery puffball bladders of many sizes grows from it, a few collapsed and brown, one breathing out a thin drift of golden dust that catches a stray beam.""",
CALM.format(plain='dark wet rock, shadow, water and haze', things='hoop, tree, skylight and bladder'),
"""LIGHT AND WEATHER. The only light is daylight from the skylights: warm sun in the shafts, soft green bounce light near them, deep cool darkness between, mist in every beam, wet highlights on the river. Colours: deep green, wet black rock, pale bone, a little dark red and gold. The mood is vast, quiet and lethal."""]
B = [HEAD.format(night='', cam='28 mm lens, deep focus', haze='sea fog building with distance', grain='slight film grain'),
"""THE PLACE. A vast tidal shelf on a cold coast at low tide, just after sunrise, sea fog burning off. The shelf is the exposed lung of a creature the size of a mountain range that died ages ago: pale bone-white rock, porous and honeycombed like weathered coral limestone, terraced, tide-stained, cut by shallow pale teal channels and pools. Set into the shelf are the open ends of its airways: round throats from five to sixty metres across. Most are only a dark hole with a low broken lip; the larger ones keep a collar of ivory cartilage built from stacked rings, eroded and incomplete. The swell drives air through them and they exhale together: a column of cold white vapour pours from each and leans the same way on the wind. Animal life, not plants, grows where the water and the breath reach: bands of crimson feathery gill-plumes along the waterline of the channels and around the throat rims, black-green weed lower down, orange crusts on the dry high rock, pale barnacle-like cones in between. The rest is bare wet bone.""",
"""VIEWPOINT AND LAYOUT, asymmetric. Seen from a ledge about six metres above a tide channel. The channel runs from the bottom centre away across the shelf in a slow S toward the far distance: the route. On the right, sixty metres away, the nearest large throat: its ringed collar, its dark opening, crimson plumes on its rim bent outward by the rush of air, its vapour column rising out of frame. In the lower left corner the edge of the ledge, wet, with one patch of crimson plumes and a tide pool. Across the middle distance four or five more throats of very different sizes, one of them quiet with only a wisp, and far beyond them dozens of thin vapour columns dissolving into a bank of fog. Three hundred metres away a loose group of five striders wades the channel: pale animals like giant sea spiders, each a small body carried eight metres up on very long thin jointed legs, small in the frame, each in a different attitude, their reflections and long shadows on the wet shelf. A flock of small dark flyers turns through one far column. At the far end, kilometres away and half lost in the fog, the coast rises into snow-streaked hills, and at their foot lies the broken end of the main windpipe: one ribbed tube of pale cartilage hundreds of metres across, on its side, collapsed and overgrown with crimson and orange, fog pouring from its dark mouth.""",
CALM.format(plain='wet bone-white rock, shallow water and fog', things='throat, vapour column, strider and patch of growth'),
"""LIGHT AND WEATHER. Backlit. The low sun is ahead and to the left, a pale disc in the fog. Everything facing the viewer is in soft cool shadow with bright warm rims; the vapour columns glow where the sun passes through them; a path of sun glitter lies on the channel; long shadows fall toward the viewer. Colours: ivory and grey-white rock, pale teal water, deep crimson in bands, wet black, small touches of orange, pale gold light. The mood is cold, quiet and lethal."""]
C = [HEAD.format(night='dusk ', cam='fast 24 mm lens at high sensitivity, available light only', haze='thin mist thickening with distance', grain='visible sensor noise in the shadows'),
"""THE PLACE. Late dusk in a long shallow valley on the body of a creature the size of a mountain range that died ages ago. Its lung has weathered open here. The valley floor is bare wet black rock, and along the stream and the seeps grow its air sacs, still alive: soft membrane bladders in bunches like frogspawn or grapes, a few to a few dozen in a bunch, from the size of a barrel to the size of a house, joined by ropes of wet tissue. They sag, wrinkle and lean on each other; some are swollen tight, some have collapsed into folds, many are dark and dead. Luminous organisms live inside the living ones, so they glow faintly and unevenly from within, cold blue-green, a few with a dim amber core, and each lit bunch throws a soft pool of light onto the mist and the wet rock around it. They exhale a thin mist that gathers in the hollows and drains downhill in slow tongues.""",
"""VIEWPOINT AND LAYOUT, asymmetric. Seen from a rise of rock about eight metres above the valley floor. A narrow black stream runs from the bottom right away down the valley, mirroring the lights: the route. In the lower left corner, close, one small bunch of three sacs on the rock, one of them collapsed, the largest showing its veins and the dark shape of something caught inside. Down the valley the bunches follow the stream at every distance, with bare dark ridges of rock between them, dimmer and bluer with distance, until the valley bends left behind a spur of cliff, where a wider glow on the mist shows that the field goes on out of sight. Halfway down, small against a lit bunch, the dark shape of a large six-legged animal walks toward the light. Swarms of tiny pale flyers hang around the nearest lights only. The far side of the valley is a dark cliff with ragged cave mouths that breathe out mist. Above the ridge the sky is deep blue-grey dusk under thin cloud, with a faint band of dull afterglow low on the horizon and no stars.""",
CALM.format(plain='dark wet rock, mist and sky', things='bunch and sac'),
"""LIGHT AND EXPOSURE. Exposed for the living light, so most of the frame is dark and quiet: blue-black land, soft cyan-green pools of light with real fall-off on mist, rock and water, a few amber points, the last cold skylight on the wet rock. The mood is silent, beautiful and lethal."""]
for k, parts in {'A-est-v4': A, 'B-est-v4': B, 'C-est-v4': C}.items():
    open(f'{R}/{k}.txt', 'w').write('\n\n'.join(parts) + '\n\n' + TAIL + '\n'); print(k, sum(map(len, parts)))
